<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-056> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Eohippus→Equus skull transformation (Fig. 401-402) (Equidae lateral skull landmarks + gallery specimen anchors)",
        "Thompson (1917) Eohippus→Equus skull transformation (Fig. 401-402) faithfully reproduces Equidae lateral skull landmarks + gallery specimen anchors morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-056-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-056-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-t1917-056-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-056_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Equidae lateral skull landmarks + gallery specimen anchors specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-056_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py> ;
    schema:about "Equidae lateral skull landmarks + gallery specimen anchors" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Direct validation of Wisniewski & Slater phylogenetic CREA deviation (Dryad not vendored)",
        "does_not_claim: That modern fossil equid series lie on a single Thompson grid without residual clade effects",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Shuffled-label and lambda sweeps; KS distance null; gallery CV masks",
        "reconstructed_in_script: TPS phi on 18 digitised landmarks; phi_t stage predictions vs drawn intermediates",
        "reported_in_source: Eohippus and Equus skulls related by coordinate deformation (Fig. 401)",
        "reported_in_source: Heilmann intermediates on the transformation (Fig. 402)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-056_on-the-theory-of-transformations.py; output: docs/media/t1917_056_on_the_theory_of_transformatio_comparison.png; organism: Equidae lateral skull landmarks + gallery specimen anchors; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.x, scipy 1.x, matplotlib 3.x, Pillow 11.x; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Eohippus and Equus skulls related by coordinate deformation (Fig. 401) | Heilmann intermediates on the transformation (Fig. 402); reconstructed_in_script: TPS phi on 18 digitised landmarks; phi_t stage predictions vs drawn intermediates | Shuffled-label and lambda sweeps; KS distance null; gallery CV masks; does_not_claim: Direct validation of Wisniewski & Slater phylogenetic CREA deviation (Dryad not vendored) | That modern fossil equid series lie on a single Thompson grid without residual clade effects]; other sources: On Growth and Form, Ch. XVII, pp. 765-767, Figs. 401-402 <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2026.10096>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.crjdfn3g3> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-056-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-056-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-056-morphometric-validation>,
